1
00:00:01,335 --> 00:00:02,503
HEY, GUYS, GUESS WHAT?

2
00:00:02,544 --> 00:00:05,046
BARRY AND MINDY ARE
GETTING A DIVORCE.

3
00:00:05,088 --> 00:00:06,173
( exclamations )

4
00:00:06,214 --> 00:00:08,676
WHAT IS THE MATTER WITH YOU?!

5
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:13,096
NO-- BARRY AND MINDY.

6
00:00:13,138 --> 00:00:14,473
OH. SORRY.

7
00:00:14,515 --> 00:00:16,600
I HEAR DIVORCE, I
IMMEDIATELY GO TO ROSS.

8
00:00:17,685 --> 00:00:19,478
WHO-WHO'S BARRY AND MINDY?

9
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,438
BARRY WAS THE GUY
THAT I ALMOST MARRIED

10
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:22,982
AND MINDY WAS MY BEST FRIEND.

11
00:00:23,022 --> 00:00:24,817
WASN'T HE CHEATING
ON YOU WITH HER?

12
00:00:24,859 --> 00:00:26,527
YEAH, BUT THAT JUST MEANS

13
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:28,445
THAT HE WAS FALLING ASLEEP
ON TOP OF HER INSTEAD OF ME.

14
00:00:28,487 --> 00:00:29,989
AH.

15
00:00:30,029 --> 00:00:32,115
GOD, COULD YOU IMAGINE
IF I'D ACTUALLY MARRIED HIM?

16
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:33,659
HOW DIFFERENT WOULD MY LIFE BE?

17
00:00:33,701 --> 00:00:35,202
Ross:
I KNOW WHAT
YOU MEAN.

18
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:37,371
I'VE ALWAYS WONDERED
HOW DIFFERENT MY LIFE WOULD BE

19
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:38,789
IF I'D NEVER GOTTEN DIVORCED.

20
00:00:38,831 --> 00:00:40,958
WHICH TIME?
THE FIRST TIME.

21
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,251
NO, SERIOUSLY,
IMAGINE IF CAROL

22
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:45,253
HADN'T REALIZED
SHE WAS A LESBIAN.

23
00:00:47,339 --> 00:00:48,716
I CAN'T.

24
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:51,677
I KEEP SEEING IT THE GOOD WAY.

25
00:00:51,719 --> 00:00:54,596
I BET I'D STILL BE DOING
MY KARA-TE.

26
00:00:55,973 --> 00:00:59,476
TOWARDS THE END OF OUR MARRIAGE,
I WAS DOING A LOT OF KARATE

27
00:00:59,518 --> 00:01:01,436
AS A WAY
OF RELEASING THE TENSION

28
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:04,231
FROM, YOU KNOW, NOT DOING
ANYTHING ELSE PHYSICAL.

29
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:05,357
MAYBE THE PROBLEM WAS

30
00:01:05,399 --> 00:01:06,942
YOU WERE PRONOUNCING
IT "KARA-TE."

31
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:09,987
WHAT IF I WAS STILL FAT?

32
00:01:10,029 --> 00:01:13,073
Y-YOU WOULDN'T BE DATING ME,
THAT'S FOR SURE.

33
00:01:13,114 --> 00:01:14,491
SURE I WOULD.

34
00:01:14,533 --> 00:01:15,951
OH, YEAH.
OH, COME ON.

35
00:01:15,993 --> 00:01:18,537
WHAT? YOU GUYS
REALLY THINK I'M
THAT SHALLOW?

36
00:01:18,579 --> 00:01:20,497
NO, I JUST THINK
MONICA WAS THAT FAT.

37
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:24,919
HEY, IMAGINE
IF I'D NEVER GOT FIRED

38
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:26,545
OFF DAYS OF OUR LIVES.

39
00:01:26,587 --> 00:01:28,756
HEY, HEY, THERE'S CAROL AGAIN.

40
00:01:30,049 --> 00:01:32,843
WHAT IF I HAD HAD THE
GUTS TO QUIT MY JOB?

41
00:01:32,885 --> 00:01:34,929
I'D PROBABLY BE WRITING
FOR THE NEW YORKER--

42
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:36,931
BEING PAID TO BE FUNNY.

43
00:01:36,972 --> 00:01:38,891
BUT MY JOB'S FUN, TOO.

44
00:01:38,933 --> 00:01:43,437
I MEAN... TOMORROW, I...
I DON'T HAVE TO WEAR A TIE.

45
00:01:43,478 --> 00:01:45,940
WHAT IF I HAD TAKEN THAT JOB
AT MERRILL LYNCH?

46
00:01:45,981 --> 00:01:46,941
WHAT?
WHAT?

47
00:01:46,982 --> 00:01:48,442
MERRILL LYNCH?

48
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:50,444
YEAH. I HAD A MASSAGE CLIENT
WHO WORKED THERE

49
00:01:50,485 --> 00:01:52,487
AND HE SAID
I HAD A KNACK FOR STOCKS.

50
00:01:52,529 --> 00:01:53,906
WHY DIDN'T YOU
TAKE THE JOB?

51
00:01:53,948 --> 00:01:55,616
BECAUSE AT THAT TIME, YOU SEE

52
00:01:55,657 --> 00:01:58,243
I THOUGHT THAT EVERYTHING
THAT RHYMED WAS TRUE.

53
00:01:58,285 --> 00:02:00,996
SO, I THOUGHT, YOU KNOW,
IF I WORKED WITH STOCKS

54
00:02:01,038 --> 00:02:03,457
I'D HAVE TO LIVE IN A BOX
AND ONLY EAT LOX

55
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:04,708
AND HAVE A PET FOX...

56
00:02:06,085 --> 00:02:08,545
HEY, DO YOU GUYS THINK
IF ALL THOSE THINGS HAPPENED

57
00:02:08,587 --> 00:02:10,047
WE'D STILL HANG OUT?

58
00:02:17,512 --> 00:02:21,976
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

59
00:02:22,017 --> 00:02:24,812
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

60
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:28,482
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

61
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:31,986
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

62
00:02:32,027 --> 00:02:34,488
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

63
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:36,740
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

64
00:02:36,782 --> 00:02:40,494
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

65
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:44,372
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

66
00:02:55,216 --> 00:02:56,844
OH, MY GOD.
RACHEL GREEN?

67
00:02:56,885 --> 00:02:57,970
( gasping )

68
00:02:58,012 --> 00:02:59,178
ROB TILLMAN.

69
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,221
NO...

70
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:01,556
( embarrassed chuckle )

71
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:03,058
NO, NO, IT'S ME, ROSS.

72
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:06,520
OH! I'M SORRY--
ROSS TILLMAN. OH!

73
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:08,689
NO. NO, NO.

74
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:09,815
ROSS GELLER.

75
00:03:09,857 --> 00:03:10,983
OH, OF COURSE!

76
00:03:11,025 --> 00:03:12,484
MONICA'S BROTHER!

77
00:03:12,526 --> 00:03:13,944
YEAH, RIGHT.

78
00:03:13,986 --> 00:03:15,236
WOW! HOW ARE YOU?!

79
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:17,364
GOOD. GOO...
I'M, I'M MARRIED.

80
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:18,573
OH. ME, TOO.

81
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:19,741
OH. WELL, OH...

82
00:03:19,783 --> 00:03:20,951
ISN'T IT THE BEST?

83
00:03:20,993 --> 00:03:23,120
OH, IT'S THE BEST.

84
00:03:23,162 --> 00:03:24,872
( sighing simultaneously )

85
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:27,248
SO, UM, HOW'S MONICA?

86
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:28,917
OH, REALLY,
REALLY GREAT.

87
00:03:28,959 --> 00:03:30,418
ACTUALLY, SHE'S RIGHT
DOWN THE STREET.

88
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:32,253
UM, DO YOU...?
YOU KNOW WHAT?

89
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:34,255
YOU SHOULD STOP
BY AND SAY HI.

90
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:35,674
OH, I WOULD LOVE TO.

91
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:37,134
OH, OH, SHE'D BE SO EXCITED.

92
00:03:37,176 --> 00:03:38,760
OH, OKAY.
COME ON.

93
00:03:38,802 --> 00:03:42,097
WAIT. DON'T YOU HAVE TO PAY
FOR YOUR... BUSTY LADIES?

94
00:03:45,266 --> 00:03:46,810
NO, NO, NO, T-THAT'S OKAY.

95
00:03:46,852 --> 00:03:49,604
SOME, SOME KID ASKED ME
TO PICK IT UP FOR HIM

96
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:50,647
( laughing ):
BUT I...

97
00:03:50,689 --> 00:03:51,690
( laughing ):
OH, OKAY.

98
00:03:58,238 --> 00:03:59,614
SO, MONICA

99
00:03:59,656 --> 00:04:02,117
STILL GOING OUT WITH
DR. BORING, HUH?

100
00:04:02,159 --> 00:04:04,285
HE'S NOT BORING.

101
00:04:04,327 --> 00:04:05,996
HE'S JUST...

102
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:10,084
HE'S JUST LOW KEY.

103
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:11,585
HERE WE GO.

104
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:12,627
ONE HAZELNUT LATTE.

105
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:13,628
THANK YOU.

106
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:14,755
YOU KNOW

107
00:04:14,796 --> 00:04:18,425
THE HAZELNUT--
ACTUALLY NOT A NUT.

108
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:20,301
IT'S A SEED.

109
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:22,804
WOW.

110
00:04:22,846 --> 00:04:25,432
CAN ANYONE ELSE
NAME A WELL-KNOWN SEED

111
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:27,809
THAT'S BEEN MASQUERADING
AS A NUT?

112
00:04:27,851 --> 00:04:31,021
OH, DEAR GOD, LET ME THINK.

113
00:04:31,063 --> 00:04:32,231
HEY.

114
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:33,565
Joey:
HEY.

115
00:04:33,607 --> 00:04:35,525
OH, NO. WHAT'S THE MATTER?

116
00:04:35,567 --> 00:04:37,485
I JUST GOT
ANOTHER REJECTION LETTER.

117
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:40,989
THEY SAID MY WRITING WAS FUNNY,
JUST NOT "ARCHIE COMIC FUNNY."

118
00:04:41,031 --> 00:04:42,282
YOU KNOW WHAT, HONEY?

119
00:04:42,323 --> 00:04:44,243
I GOT TO GET BACK
TO THE HOSPITAL.

120
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:45,493
ALL RIGHT. MMM.

121
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:47,121
OKAY.
BYE.

122
00:04:47,162 --> 00:04:48,247
OH, UH...

123
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:50,457
BY THE WAY, THE ANSWER IS...

124
00:04:50,498 --> 00:04:51,959
THE BRAZIL NUT.

125
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,503
AH.

126
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:57,672
WAS HIS QUESTION
"WHAT'S MORE BORING THAN HIM?"

127
00:04:59,049 --> 00:05:01,509
HEY, MAN, LOOK,
SORRY ABOUT THAT ARCHIE THING.

128
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:03,386
YOU NEED ME
TO GIVE YOU SOME MONEY?

129
00:05:03,428 --> 00:05:07,515
HEY, I MAY HAVE NO MONEY,
BUT I STILL HAVE MY PRIDE.

130
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,434
REALLY?

131
00:05:11,228 --> 00:05:12,854
EH...

132
00:05:12,896 --> 00:05:16,024
HEY, MAYBE JOEY DOESN'T HAVE
TO GIVE YOU THE MONEY.

133
00:05:16,066 --> 00:05:17,776
TV STARS HAVE ASSISTANTS,
RIGHT?

134
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:19,444
THAT'S AN IDEA.

135
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:22,572
HEY, IF I HIRED AN ASSISTANT,
WOULD YOU TAKE MONEY FROM HER?

136
00:05:22,614 --> 00:05:23,865
NO, JOEY.

137
00:05:23,907 --> 00:05:25,575
CHANDLER COULD BE
YOUR ASSISTANT.

138
00:05:25,617 --> 00:05:28,203
SEE, HE COULD ANSWER
ALL YOUR FAN MAIL AND STUFF.

139
00:05:28,245 --> 00:05:29,370
THAT WOULD BE GREAT.

140
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:30,580
LET'S DO THAT.

141
00:05:30,622 --> 00:05:32,707
IT COULD GIVE ME TIME TO WRITE.

142
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:34,251
ALL RIGHT, GREAT.
WELCOME ABOARD.

143
00:05:34,293 --> 00:05:35,252
OKAY.
ALL RIGHT.

144
00:05:35,294 --> 00:05:36,544
I NEED TO USE THE BATHROOM

145
00:05:36,586 --> 00:05:38,297
AND SINCE I DON'T NEED
ASSISTANCE IN THERE

146
00:05:38,337 --> 00:05:40,299
TAKE A BREAK!

147
00:05:40,339 --> 00:05:41,883
ALL RIGHT.

148
00:05:41,925 --> 00:05:44,011
HEY.

149
00:05:44,052 --> 00:05:45,262
Monica:
HEY, PHOEBE.

150
00:05:45,304 --> 00:05:46,596
GUESS WHAT?
WHAT?

151
00:05:46,638 --> 00:05:48,723
JOEY JUST HIRED CHANDLER
TO BE HIS ASSISTANT.

152
00:05:48,765 --> 00:05:49,808
OH, THAT'S SO SWEET.

153
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:50,892
( phone ringing )

154
00:05:50,934 --> 00:05:51,935
OH! HANG ON!

155
00:05:51,977 --> 00:05:54,604
HANG ON!

156
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:57,774
( ringing continues )

157
00:05:57,816 --> 00:05:59,609
GO.

158
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:01,278
NO. NO, NO.

159
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,488
I SAID SELL WHEN IT HITS 50.

160
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:05,406
FIVE-"O". IT'S A NUMBER.

161
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:07,408
IT COMES AFTER FOUR-NINE.

162
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:09,077
OH, IT'S OKAY. IT'S OKAY.

163
00:06:09,119 --> 00:06:10,954
YOU'RE ALLOWED ONE MISTAKE.

164
00:06:10,996 --> 00:06:12,080
JUST KIDDING.

165
00:06:12,122 --> 00:06:13,290
YOU ARE, OF COURSE, FIRED.

166
00:06:15,374 --> 00:06:16,960
OH...!

167
00:06:17,002 --> 00:06:18,212
HEY, MON. MON.

168
00:06:18,253 --> 00:06:20,005
LOOK WHO I RAN INTO.

169
00:06:20,047 --> 00:06:21,173
( gasping )

170
00:06:21,215 --> 00:06:23,300
OH, MY GOD! RACHEL!

171
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:28,263
GOSH, YOU LOOK TERRIFIC!

172
00:06:28,305 --> 00:06:29,973
OH, SO DO YOU!

173
00:06:30,015 --> 00:06:31,516
( laughing )

174
00:06:31,558 --> 00:06:32,934
DID YOU LOSE WEIGHT?

175
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:34,602
YOU'RE SO SWEET TO NOTICE!

176
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,771
YES, I LOST
THREE-AND-A-HALF POUNDS!

177
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:37,981
AH!

178
00:06:38,023 --> 00:06:40,359
( laughing )

179
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:42,527
AND, UH, YOU REMEMBER
MY FRIEND CHANDLER.

180
00:06:42,569 --> 00:06:45,072
AND, UH,
AND THAT'S PHOEBE OVER THERE.

181
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:45,947
HI.

182
00:06:45,989 --> 00:06:47,366
OH, MY GOD!
SIT DOWN.

183
00:06:47,406 --> 00:06:49,951
HOW LONG HAS IT BEEN
SINCE WE'VE SEEN EACH OTHER?

184
00:06:49,993 --> 00:06:51,119
1987--

185
00:06:51,161 --> 00:06:52,453
THE DAY AFTER CHRISTMAS.

186
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:53,621
SHAUN McMAHAN'S PARTY.

187
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:55,249
I PLAYED YOU
ONE OF MY SONGS--

188
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:56,415
YOU KNOW, UH

189
00:06:56,457 --> 00:06:58,293
"INTERPLANETARY
COURTSHIP RITUAL."

190
00:06:59,669 --> 00:07:01,338
OH, YEAH.

191
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:02,589
RIGHT.

192
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,465
SO, UH, DO YOU
STILL DO MUSIC?

193
00:07:04,507 --> 00:07:05,508
WELL, SOMETIMES.

194
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:06,551
YOU SHOULD COME OVER.

195
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:07,844
I'LL PLAY YOU
ONE OF MY...

196
00:07:07,886 --> 00:07:09,096
OH, MY GOD!

197
00:07:09,137 --> 00:07:12,766
JOEY TRIBBIANI
FROM DAYS OF OUR LIVES

198
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:14,976
JUST WALKED IN HERE.

199
00:07:15,018 --> 00:07:16,311
RACH, HE'S A FRIEND OF OURS.

200
00:07:16,353 --> 00:07:19,398
YOU ARE FRIENDS
WITH DR. DRAKE RAMORAY?

201
00:07:19,438 --> 00:07:20,941
MM-HMM.

202
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:23,484
WELL, IT'S KIND OF HARD
TO BE FRIENDS WITH DRAKE

203
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:26,821
BECAUSE OF HIS BUSY SCHEDULE,
AND THE FACT THAT HE'S NOT REAL.

204
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:31,826
HEY, HEY, OR I COULD BRING
MY KEYBOARD HERE SOMETIME.

205
00:07:31,868 --> 00:07:33,494
HE'S COMING OVER,
HE'S COMING OVER.

206
00:07:33,536 --> 00:07:35,038
JOEY...
I KNOW. HERE, HERE.

207
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:36,664
OH...!

208
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:37,874
NO.

209
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:39,500
THIS IS MY FRIEND, RACHEL.

210
00:07:39,542 --> 00:07:41,420
WE WENT TO HIGH SCHOOL
TOGETHER.

211
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:42,670
( hysterical laugh )

212
00:07:42,712 --> 00:07:43,838
HI.
HI!

213
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:47,217
I LOVE YOU ON THAT SHOW!

214
00:07:47,259 --> 00:07:48,260
OH...

215
00:07:48,302 --> 00:07:49,552
I WATCH YOU
EVERY DAY.

216
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:51,930
I MEAN, WHEN YOU TOOK
OUT YOUR OWN KIDNEY

217
00:07:51,972 --> 00:07:53,181
TO SAVE YOUR EX-WIFE

218
00:07:53,223 --> 00:07:55,474
EVEN THOUGH SHE
TRIED TO KILL YOU...

219
00:07:55,516 --> 00:07:58,061
WELL, IT'S ALWAYS NICE
TO MEET THE FANS.

220
00:07:58,103 --> 00:07:59,229
AH...!

221
00:07:59,271 --> 00:08:00,605
SHE'S NOT CRAZY, IS SHE?

222
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:01,940
NO, SHE'S COOL.

223
00:08:01,982 --> 00:08:03,275
SO, UH...

224
00:08:03,317 --> 00:08:05,193
HOW YOU DOING?

225
00:08:05,235 --> 00:08:06,820
( hysterical giggles )

226
00:08:10,949 --> 00:08:12,409
( phone ringing )

227
00:08:12,451 --> 00:08:13,785
HANG ON.

228
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:16,079
HANG ON.

229
00:08:16,121 --> 00:08:19,124
HANG ON.

230
00:08:19,166 --> 00:08:20,375
GO.

231
00:08:20,417 --> 00:08:22,002
WHO IS THIS?

232
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:24,087
OH, OKAY. YOU'RE GOING
TO LIKE WORKING FOR ME.

233
00:08:24,129 --> 00:08:25,380
WHAT'S YOUR NAME?

234
00:08:25,422 --> 00:08:28,300
WHAT KIND OF NAME IS BRINDY?

235
00:08:28,342 --> 00:08:31,803
I... WHATEVE... STOP TALKING.

236
00:08:31,845 --> 00:08:35,515
ALL RIGHT, FROM NOW ON,
YOUR NAME IS JOAN.

237
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:37,600
YOU CAN PICK YOUR OWN LAST NAME.

238
00:08:38,977 --> 00:08:40,937
HEY, THERE YOU ARE.

239
00:08:40,979 --> 00:08:42,897
UH-OH, IT'S MY BOSS.

240
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:44,941
ALL RIGHT,
HERE'S A LIST OF THINGS

241
00:08:44,983 --> 00:08:46,234
FOR YOU TO DO TODAY.

242
00:08:46,276 --> 00:08:47,861
MAN, THIS IS GOING
TO BE SO GREAT.

243
00:08:47,902 --> 00:08:48,862
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

244
00:08:48,903 --> 00:08:50,697
I GOT TO GO TO WORK.

245
00:08:50,738 --> 00:08:53,116
I'M DELIVERING TWINS TODAY,
BUT ONLY ONE OF THEM... IS MINE.

246
00:08:53,158 --> 00:08:54,326
( snaps fingers )

247
00:08:56,495 --> 00:08:57,871
